WEBVTT

00:03.470 --> 00:06.907
Imperial Calendar Year 955

00:06.907 --> 00:11.245
As a result of the battle triggered
by the Triple Alliance's invasion...

00:11.245 --> 00:17.918
...the Humankind Abh Empire
began a huge retaliation.

00:17.918 --> 00:21.822
This retaliation was known as
Operation Phantom Flame.

00:21.822 --> 00:25.359
The Star Forces fleet of
Operation Phantom Flame...

00:25.359 --> 00:32.766
...has established a stronghold
in the enemy's territory.

00:32.766 --> 00:33.634
However, in response to
the Alliance's counterattack...

00:33.634 --> 00:36.704
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
However, in response to
the Alliance's counterattack...

00:36.704 --> 00:40.307
Commander-in-Chief
Commanding Admiral Abriel
...Operation Phantom Flame
has entered a new phase...

00:40.307 --> 00:41.075
...in which the objective is
to annihilate the enemy fleet.

00:41.075 --> 00:43.677
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
...in which the objective is
to annihilate the enemy fleet.

00:43.677 --> 00:45.379
First Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral Spoor
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:45.379 --> 00:46.113
They await the Triple Alliance
in the Aptic System...

00:46.113 --> 00:50.413
Second Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rulef
...soon to be the main battlefield.

00:50.651 --> 00:51.085
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:51.085 --> 00:55.222
Fourth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Kotoponi
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:55.222 --> 00:56.190
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:56.190 --> 00:57.191
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
While the size of the enemy fleet
is expected to be 170 squadrons...

00:57.191 --> 01:00.327
Fifth Fleet Commander-in-Chief
Admiral of the Fleet Rekef
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:00.327 --> 01:01.128
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:01.128 --> 01:04.291
Aptic Defense Fleet Commander
Admiral Bebaus
...the defense forces of Admiral
Bebaus consist of only twelve squadrons.

01:04.765 --> 01:09.670
Given that they are outnumbered
by almost fifteen-to-one...

01:09.670 --> 01:13.606
...the two fleets have decided on
the time of the decisive battle.

01:17.077 --> 01:18.442
It has started.

01:18.879 --> 01:21.548
The enemy mines at the
head of the formation...

01:21.548 --> 01:23.379
...approaching fast!

01:25.419 --> 01:26.408
Commence battle!

01:31.859 --> 01:34.528
So, first on the scene
is the Basroil.

01:34.528 --> 01:36.996
They sure have a lot of
energy and enthusiasm.

01:37.631 --> 01:40.532
An enemy mine will be within
firing range in ten seconds.

01:41.135 --> 01:43.837
Eight... seven... six...

01:43.837 --> 01:47.574
...five... four... three... two...

01:47.574 --> 01:48.642
...one.

01:48.642 --> 01:50.269
Enemy mine within firing range!

01:55.315 --> 01:56.873
Fire the anti-proton cannon!

02:00.988 --> 02:02.421
It split in two?!

02:05.726 --> 02:06.493
It's still active!

02:06.493 --> 02:07.694
This is it, huh?!

02:07.694 --> 02:09.321
Those mines we saw at Wimpel!

02:12.099 --> 02:12.929
Ekuryua!

02:13.667 --> 02:14.326
Firing!

02:21.642 --> 02:23.200
What the hell...?!

02:29.983 --> 02:31.051
We're surrounded!

02:31.051 --> 02:33.281
Keep firing! Don't ease up!

02:36.824 --> 02:38.058
Ekuryua! Watch out behind!

02:38.058 --> 02:39.650
Five and seven!
Firing!

02:46.733 --> 02:48.402
Port side armor has been damaged!

02:48.402 --> 02:51.672
There's also damage in
Sectors 4, 11 and 15.

02:51.672 --> 02:52.900
And now Sector 7, too!

02:53.874 --> 02:55.275
What about casualties?

02:55.275 --> 02:56.401
Everyone's okay at the moment.

02:57.044 --> 02:59.113
Onboard temperature is rising.

02:59.113 --> 03:01.115
I don't think we
need to be worried.

03:01.115 --> 03:02.549
It's probably just temporary.

03:02.549 --> 03:04.176
Basroil, are you still together?!

03:04.952 --> 03:06.086
We can continue.

03:06.086 --> 03:07.588
So this is what was on the report.

03:07.588 --> 03:08.452
I believe so.

03:09.022 --> 03:10.512
There's a second wave coming!

03:18.665 --> 03:22.260
Shooting Star

03:28.008 --> 03:32.445
Banner of the Stars

04:52.392 --> 04:54.883
How many mines did the
enemy bring with them?

04:55.462 --> 04:59.023
You'd think they would save
some for the main fleet battle.

04:59.800 --> 05:01.401
Even if they were to defeat us...

05:01.401 --> 05:03.237
...and then establish themselves
in the Aptic region...

05:03.237 --> 05:04.829
...they'd still need more mines.

05:06.440 --> 05:08.499
Why don't you explain that to them?

05:08.775 --> 05:11.178
I almost want to.

05:11.178 --> 05:12.975
What could they be thinking?

05:13.880 --> 05:15.382
Whatever they're thinking...

05:15.382 --> 05:17.680
...we have to hold down the fort.

05:18.051 --> 05:19.746
Let's use the mines
from the patrol ships.

05:20.153 --> 05:22.781
Weren't we saving those
for when we rout them?

05:23.257 --> 05:26.090
If we lose here, we'll never
get them on the run.

05:26.426 --> 05:29.327
Awfully practical thinking
coming from you.

05:30.330 --> 05:33.667
If that means you agree
with my rationale...

05:33.667 --> 05:35.869
...then I have to say I'm
just as surprised as you.

05:35.869 --> 05:38.405
No point in being
surprised at each other.

05:38.405 --> 05:40.498
I hate to say that I agree with you.

05:41.441 --> 05:43.443
Relay this to all patrol ships.

05:43.443 --> 05:45.411
Begin the mine counterattack.

05:46.280 --> 05:47.178
What's the matter?

05:47.681 --> 05:50.081
It looks like we're
a little late for that, Nereis.

05:53.420 --> 05:54.688
No way!

05:54.688 --> 05:56.087
What's going on?!

05:56.556 --> 05:57.284
It's their new weapon!

05:58.191 --> 05:59.593
Their new weapon?

05:59.593 --> 06:01.561
You're not fooling around,
are you?

06:18.111 --> 06:19.408
Third attack vessel squadron
eliminated!

06:20.614 --> 06:22.377
Tenth attack vessel squadron
eliminated!

06:22.849 --> 06:24.578
Eighth attack vessel squadron
eliminated!

06:25.152 --> 06:26.119
I see.

06:26.119 --> 06:28.519
The weapon mentioned
in the reconnaissance report?

06:29.222 --> 06:31.692
You're taking this badly, Nereis.

06:31.692 --> 06:33.660
About the situation here?

06:34.127 --> 06:37.028
Or that our family reputation
is at stake here?

06:38.298 --> 06:40.562
Well, it's not very good
whichever way you look at it.

06:40.901 --> 06:43.503
In any case, what about
our attack vessels?

06:43.503 --> 06:47.234
We can't just let them sit there
in the middle of a mine attack.

06:48.408 --> 06:49.676
We haven't got much choice.

06:49.676 --> 06:52.112
If the enemy sends
their attack ships in...

06:52.112 --> 06:53.670
...we'll need their help.

06:54.481 --> 06:56.550
But we've got to do something.

06:56.550 --> 06:58.151
Let's bring in the guard ships.

06:58.151 --> 06:58.640
What?

06:59.553 --> 07:02.756
We'll escort each attack squadron
with a squadron of guard ships.

07:02.756 --> 07:06.089
We can let the unit commanders
arrange their own formations.

07:06.960 --> 07:07.654
Sounds reasonable.

07:08.328 --> 07:09.496
I know.

07:09.496 --> 07:11.031
But we have little time.
Let's hurry.

07:11.031 --> 07:11.963
All right.

07:12.332 --> 07:13.663
Oh, Nefee...

07:15.068 --> 07:17.637
If we gather data from
each of the ships...

07:17.637 --> 07:20.697
...do you think we can simulate
those enemy mines?

07:21.375 --> 07:22.171
What are you getting at?

07:23.009 --> 07:25.645
We need to check
that we've destroyed...

07:25.645 --> 07:27.510
...every single one of them.

07:28.081 --> 07:31.573
Mines that haven't been
destroyed are lying in ambush.

07:32.285 --> 07:34.549
Then we can send warnings
to our ships on their positions.

07:34.955 --> 07:37.549
Does the command ship have
the capacity to coordinate that?

07:38.158 --> 07:41.361
We'll have to process
enormous amounts of data.

07:41.361 --> 07:43.556
But it's worth giving it a try.

07:43.764 --> 07:45.755
I'll ask the officer in charge
if it's possible.

07:46.800 --> 07:48.402
Communications Chief...

07:48.402 --> 07:50.570
...how long before
the main fleet arrives?

07:50.570 --> 07:51.571
Yes, sir.

07:51.571 --> 07:53.240
The schedule says...

07:53.240 --> 07:55.876
...they should arrive
in about six hours.

07:55.876 --> 07:57.639
That's a problem.

08:03.683 --> 08:05.118
If it's going according to plan...

08:05.118 --> 08:08.455
...I imagine the battle at the
Aptic Gate has already started.

08:08.455 --> 08:09.523
Is that so?

08:09.523 --> 08:13.527
It would be nice if they'd finish it
before we get there.

08:13.527 --> 08:14.761
Given their numbers...

08:14.761 --> 08:16.592
...we're at a great disadvantage.

08:17.497 --> 08:18.698
They'll need our help...

08:18.698 --> 08:21.101
...as well as that of the
main Third Fleet...

08:21.101 --> 08:22.932
...to defend Aptic successfully.

08:23.136 --> 08:25.001
What about Admiral Rulef?

08:25.238 --> 08:28.008
His main priority is still
to defend the Mystel Gate...

08:28.008 --> 08:30.670
...but it's only a matter of time
before he moves on to Aptic.

08:31.344 --> 08:35.110
The enemy is clearly focusing
their strength on Aptic.

08:36.316 --> 08:37.317
I see.

08:37.317 --> 08:40.809
Well, I suppose that means we'll
be the first ones on the scene.

08:41.021 --> 08:43.785
That's the plan, if all goes well.

08:44.291 --> 08:47.783
That reminds me. I wonder
how that Princess is doing.

08:47.994 --> 08:51.259
As I recall, she was
assigned to the Aptic region.

08:51.898 --> 08:53.331
What princess is that?

08:53.667 --> 08:56.970
Three years ago, I rescued
a pretty princess at Sufugnoff...

08:56.970 --> 09:00.428
...who looked like a little kitten
who couldn't find her way home.

09:10.450 --> 09:12.319
The port side armor...

09:12.319 --> 09:13.445
The temperature's rising!

09:20.160 --> 09:21.684
Ekuryua! Fire Four and Eight!

09:26.266 --> 09:29.064
The output of the engines
has decreased by 0.05!

09:33.006 --> 09:34.174
Ekuryua!

09:34.174 --> 09:36.877
Shoot at everything that looks
like a mine, moving or not!

09:36.877 --> 09:37.639
Yes, ma'am!

09:38.111 --> 09:40.443
It's hard enough handling
the ones that are moving.

09:47.521 --> 09:48.488
We're going to crash!

09:52.592 --> 09:54.457
What's the status with
the enemy mines?

09:54.828 --> 09:57.030
There doesn't seem to be
any more that are moving.

09:57.030 --> 09:59.658
But there's debris everywhere.

09:59.799 --> 10:01.601
If there are any dormant mines...

10:01.601 --> 10:04.593
...we'll have difficulty identifying
them until they're activated.

10:05.472 --> 10:06.439
All right.

10:06.439 --> 10:08.842
Decrease engine output by 0.2.

10:08.842 --> 10:10.332
Keep an eye out
for dormant mines.

10:10.644 --> 10:12.168
I appreciate that.

10:12.512 --> 10:14.503
Supply Officer! Damage report!

10:15.515 --> 10:17.484
The first explosion...

10:17.484 --> 10:20.186
...seems to have slightly damaged
the starboard side armor.

10:20.186 --> 10:21.915
It won't be a problem.

10:22.188 --> 10:23.757
Even if the armor was new...

10:23.757 --> 10:27.160
...it only takes one direct hit
to turn it into a ball of plasma.

10:27.160 --> 10:29.321
Everyone, stay focused.

10:29.663 --> 10:31.130
Message coming through
from Command!

10:31.565 --> 10:33.833
Good job, Basroil.

10:33.833 --> 10:35.323
What's your status?

10:36.102 --> 10:37.070
There's no problem.

10:37.070 --> 10:38.002
We can keep going.

10:50.951 --> 10:54.020
It looks like the guard ships
have started their barrage.

10:54.020 --> 10:55.647
That'll take some pressure off.

10:56.489 --> 10:58.650
I don't know if I should be
grateful or worried.

10:59.359 --> 11:01.861
Any sign of the enemy's
main fleet yet?

11:01.861 --> 11:03.129
We're not able to confirm...

11:03.129 --> 11:04.664
...but I'd say they haven't arrived.

11:04.664 --> 11:08.122
They seem to be trying to
eliminate us by using mine attacks.

11:08.735 --> 11:10.270
Mines approaching the
port side from the rear!

11:10.270 --> 11:11.304
Here they come!

11:11.304 --> 11:12.601
I'll be in contact later.

11:12.973 --> 11:13.905
Good luck!

11:14.641 --> 11:15.275
Ekuryua.

11:15.275 --> 11:15.875
How many?

11:15.875 --> 11:16.876
Three.

11:16.876 --> 11:18.434
Can we push the engines
to maximum?

11:19.279 --> 11:20.113
Yes, ma'am.

11:20.113 --> 11:22.377
We're okay. Just say the word.

11:34.794 --> 11:36.022
What are those explosions?

11:36.863 --> 11:38.832
I think it was one of our
patrol ships.

11:38.832 --> 11:42.393
A patrol ship out here would be
like a sitting duck!

11:43.370 --> 11:45.005
Well, that's what it looks like.

11:45.005 --> 11:46.472
They came in too deep.

11:47.974 --> 11:48.906
We'll go and rescue them!

11:50.043 --> 11:51.908
Inform Command and
the guard ship squadron!

12:18.905 --> 12:21.107
Enemy mine formations
confirmed in target area!

12:21.107 --> 12:23.132
Distance seventy wesdaj!

12:24.377 --> 12:26.311
Keep our distance but
continue to advance!

12:37.624 --> 12:40.060
In front! Two, four, eight...

12:40.060 --> 12:42.585
...and more!
Six, four and nine!

12:55.875 --> 12:57.577
Exterior temperature rising!

12:57.577 --> 12:59.012
Partial meltdown confirmed!

12:59.012 --> 13:01.139
Starting to affect engine output!

13:01.681 --> 13:03.979
Behind us!
Eight, three and six!

13:07.353 --> 13:08.650
We can't do it. There's too many!

13:19.399 --> 13:20.423
What was that?!

13:21.201 --> 13:22.361
It's the Kidroil!

13:24.971 --> 13:28.429
I should get a medal for
rescuing an imperial princess!

13:32.178 --> 13:34.305
Behind! Eighteen and six!

13:56.402 --> 13:58.802
It wasn't even a direct hit.

13:59.339 --> 14:01.708
Regardless, it's a mess.

14:01.708 --> 14:03.107
I doubt we can save them.

14:05.011 --> 14:06.706
Looks like we were too late.

14:22.162 --> 14:24.798
All ships of the
first attack squadron!

14:24.798 --> 14:26.866
The patrol ship is doomed.

14:26.866 --> 14:28.635
Concentrate on protecting
the Calikes!

14:28.635 --> 14:29.761
Roger!

15:13.379 --> 15:15.882
They're emitting distress signals.

15:15.882 --> 15:18.084
Calikes aren't even attack vessels.

15:18.084 --> 15:19.786
But the mines are just machines.

15:19.786 --> 15:21.688
They can't hear people scream.

15:21.688 --> 15:23.156
That's all very well...

15:23.156 --> 15:25.391
...but the United Mankind...

15:25.391 --> 15:28.292
...doesn't even consider us
Abh to be human.

15:32.866 --> 15:34.601
But I can hear them.

15:34.601 --> 15:36.870
The voices of the dying.

15:36.870 --> 15:38.201
The human voices.

15:50.416 --> 15:52.619
All ships of the
first attack squadron!

15:52.619 --> 15:55.688
Defending this region
is not our responsibility.

15:55.688 --> 15:56.882
We're retreating.

15:57.023 --> 15:58.424
But what about the Calikes?

15:58.424 --> 16:00.722
We'll leave that up to
the guard ships.

16:01.895 --> 16:03.123
Understood.

16:03.863 --> 16:05.431
The guard ships?

16:05.431 --> 16:06.733
It's too dangerous.

16:06.733 --> 16:09.361
I'm sure they know that.

16:09.469 --> 16:10.595
Pray for them.

16:11.371 --> 16:12.531
But...

16:19.913 --> 16:21.346
I suppose.

16:22.181 --> 16:24.479
We're on a battlefield here.

16:26.319 --> 16:29.311
Is the support given by
the attack ships working out?

16:30.056 --> 16:31.424
It's having some effect.

16:31.424 --> 16:34.160
Anyway, if we can launch
our mines...

16:34.160 --> 16:37.186
...we can keep the enemy mines
at bay and even force them to retreat.

16:37.297 --> 16:39.788
It's not exactly a speedy solution.

16:40.033 --> 16:41.591
What are you going to do, Nereis?

16:42.402 --> 16:45.337
I'm surprised you haven't
got any suggestions, Nefee.

16:46.973 --> 16:49.742
Why don't we pull back
the attack vessels...

16:49.742 --> 16:51.232
...and bring the guard ships forward?

16:51.444 --> 16:53.446
Tell the guard ships to get rid of...

16:53.446 --> 16:56.149
...anything that looks suspicious...

16:56.149 --> 16:58.351
...while keeping
the assault ships close.

16:58.351 --> 16:59.953
Once the enemy attacks...

16:59.953 --> 17:02.649
...it will be the guard ships
that are in trouble.

17:03.923 --> 17:05.948
All right. Seems ordinary.

17:06.893 --> 17:09.862
I always find your praise
very comforting, brother.

17:09.862 --> 17:11.731
Well, issue the orders.

17:11.731 --> 17:12.629
Right away.

17:22.575 --> 17:24.610
The port side armor
has been hit badly!

17:24.610 --> 17:26.412
All damaged sectors sealed!

17:26.412 --> 17:29.716
The pressure leak
has been stopped.

17:29.716 --> 17:31.784
We have one wounded
in the engine room!

17:31.784 --> 17:32.842
Wh-Who is it?!

17:33.152 --> 17:34.210
Mento Kran!

17:35.822 --> 17:36.823
Paveryua!

17:36.823 --> 17:38.758
The engine output's
been decreasing!

17:38.758 --> 17:40.526
It was that barrage!

17:40.526 --> 17:42.562
Give us another twenty seconds!

17:42.562 --> 17:43.896
Okay!

17:43.896 --> 17:45.193
How's Kran doing?

17:45.932 --> 17:47.593
He's the one doing the repairs!

17:49.302 --> 17:51.099
Don't worry. He's invincible!

17:51.771 --> 17:52.839
Good.

17:52.839 --> 17:55.708
Engine output has
recovered to 0. 95!

17:55.708 --> 17:57.107
Over to you, Line Wing Aviator!

17:58.111 --> 17:59.908
We're back up, Captain!

18:00.313 --> 18:01.439
Good work.

18:05.852 --> 18:08.480
What's going on with
our mine counterattack?!

18:12.558 --> 18:14.727
Port side temperature is rising!

18:14.727 --> 18:16.629
That explosion came pretty close!

18:16.629 --> 18:18.756
No damage to the armor!

18:19.766 --> 18:21.757
I wish they'd cut it out!

18:28.574 --> 18:30.610
I've kept you waiting, Nereis.

18:30.610 --> 18:31.975
The frontline ships are ready.

18:33.079 --> 18:34.881
Launch immediately.

18:34.881 --> 18:36.678
Let's push those enemy mines.

18:49.328 --> 18:51.888
Captain!
Three enemy mines approaching!

18:52.932 --> 18:55.168
Mines from our side
will soon retaliate!

18:55.168 --> 18:56.903
We're almost out of danger.

18:56.903 --> 18:57.892
Concentrate!

19:08.114 --> 19:09.411
Mines from starboard!

19:10.550 --> 19:12.585
The Kidroil's coming in
to our port side.

19:12.585 --> 19:14.450
It looks like they're
positioning to retaliate!

19:14.787 --> 19:15.721
But Captain...

19:15.721 --> 19:18.324
...there're three enemy mines
coming directly behind them!

19:18.324 --> 19:19.625
Do they know that?

19:19.625 --> 19:21.650
Yes. They are firing at them.

19:22.528 --> 19:23.529
Right!

19:23.529 --> 19:24.621
Let's offer support!

19:27.733 --> 19:28.634
Just two left!

19:28.634 --> 19:29.965
Hurry up and finish the job!

19:32.538 --> 19:33.973
The Princess.

19:33.973 --> 19:36.373
So much for doing her a favor.

19:48.921 --> 19:49.580
Did we get them?

19:51.224 --> 19:52.122
Not yet!

20:04.504 --> 20:05.471
Damage report!

20:05.872 --> 20:09.273
Major damage to the starboard rear,
and a wing has been sheared off.

20:09.642 --> 20:11.043
Interior pressure is dropping fast!

20:11.043 --> 20:14.274
Explosions reported in
sectors 13 to 22.

20:14.680 --> 20:16.315
Things are starting to explode!

20:16.315 --> 20:17.450
Oh, no!

20:17.450 --> 20:19.185
Temperature in the
engine room is rising!

20:19.185 --> 20:21.554
The output is down to 0. 1!

20:21.554 --> 20:23.385
Now, to 0.05!

20:23.589 --> 20:24.123
Captain!

20:24.123 --> 20:25.750
More mines directly ahead!

20:26.726 --> 20:27.994
Shoot them down!

20:27.994 --> 20:28.728
We can't!

20:28.728 --> 20:29.660
The cannons are out!

20:42.675 --> 20:44.040
Message from Command.

20:44.944 --> 20:46.707
Our mines are on their way.

20:47.079 --> 20:49.479
They can distinguish us
from the enemy, but be careful!

20:50.550 --> 20:51.384
They're here!

20:51.384 --> 20:52.544
Our mines!

21:14.507 --> 21:15.701
They are almost like...

21:19.879 --> 21:21.676
...the souls.

21:41.367 --> 21:42.698
Finally.

21:43.069 --> 21:44.303
Yes.

21:44.303 --> 21:46.138
We can buy a little time now.

21:46.138 --> 21:47.935
I'm sure the guard ships
are relieved.

21:49.041 --> 21:51.942
But we did take quite a lot of hits.

21:52.712 --> 21:56.011
And to think the enemy's main
fleet is still in that region.

21:56.649 --> 21:58.351
Why don't we...

21:58.351 --> 22:01.721
...just make our way through
that gate into Plane Space...

22:01.721 --> 22:04.451
...and let our fleets battle it out
to the very end.

22:04.991 --> 22:06.425
That's stupid.

22:06.425 --> 22:09.656
If we do that we'll
certainly be wiped out.

22:10.162 --> 22:13.733
Maybe I'm starting to show
signs of the famous...

22:13.733 --> 22:16.065
...Spectacular Insanity
of the Bebaus family.

22:28.347 --> 22:31.009
This battlefield has already
taken countless lives.

22:31.517 --> 22:32.677
But...

22:33.052 --> 22:35.680
But we've still to catch
sight of the enemy fleet!

22:36.622 --> 22:38.146
The real battle...

22:39.091 --> 22:40.820
...hasn't begun yet.

22:42.762 --> 22:47.825
Arrival of the main fleet...
five hours to go.

22:49.368 --> 22:52.895
kizukanai koto ga
The things I did not notice

22:54.340 --> 22:58.208
konnani takusan aru
I didn't know there were so many

22:59.812 --> 23:03.407
kyoumade no jibun ga
I think of myself until today

23:04.717 --> 23:08.312
nasakenaku omoete
To be so pathetic

23:08.621 --> 23:10.823
kuyashii kurai
It's almost frustrating

23:10.823 --> 23:14.190
haritsumeta kimochi ga
This tense feeling

23:16.095 --> 23:21.267
massugu ni muite ireba
As long as I keep facing forward

23:21.267 --> 23:24.600
setsunasa no nukumori
This momentary warmth

23:25.271 --> 23:28.866
hajimete shitta
I understood it for the first time

23:29.875 --> 23:34.246
kimi ga iruto
When you are there

23:34.246 --> 23:41.587
itsumo pink no namida ga nagareteru
The pink tears are always flowing

23:41.587 --> 23:46.859
kono mune no naka wo afureteru
My heart is brimming with it

23:46.859 --> 23:55.597
kimi ga dokoni itemo dareto hanashitemo
Wherever you are and whoever you talk to

23:57.269 --> 24:02.575
issho ni itaiyo soba ni ite
I want to be with you, to be near you

24:02.575 --> 24:07.546
tsunaida te kara yubisaki kara
From our linked hands and our finger tips

24:07.546 --> 24:15.976
karadajuu no omoi binetsu tsutawatte
My body heat transmits the feelings inside

24:16.422 --> 24:20.688
tomerarenai
And I cannot stop it

24:31.337 --> 24:32.004
Commander!

24:32.004 --> 24:33.873
My ship can still fight!

24:33.873 --> 24:37.639
This is the battle you've
all been waiting for!

24:40.413 --> 24:43.109
Ship's temperature rising!
A danger of armor meltdown!

24:45.251 --> 24:46.946
Lafiel! We're too far away!

24:48.554 --> 24:50.454
Now it's four against four.

24:52.792 --> 24:55.352
I've never...

24:55.995 --> 24:57.863
...I've never lost in jousting!

24:57.863 --> 25:00.798
Next Episode...
The Flaming Battlefield
